# Template for secrets.yaml (gitignored) in this same directory.
# scripts/write-secrets.sh (the `write-secrets` nx target, run before every
# build) generates secrets.yaml from it, taking each key from
# BASEMENT_LIGHTS_DASHBOARD_<UPPERCASED_KEY> in the environment or in
# apps/basement-lights-dashboard/.env. A hand-written secrets.yaml is never
# overwritten. See README.md "Secrets".
#
# No station wifi credentials here on purpose: the device gets those via its
# (open, unpassworded) captive-portal setup flow at first boot instead.

# Native API encryption key (32 bytes, base64). Generate your own with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Enter this same value in HA when it prompts for the encryption key while
# adding the discovered device under Settings > Devices & Services.
# The real key is this panel's own (never shared with other apps):
# BASEMENT_LIGHTS_DASHBOARD_API_ENCRYPTION_KEY, kept in bws as
# basement-lights-dashboard/BASEMENT_LIGHTS_DASHBOARD_API_ENCRYPTION_KEY and as
# the same-named GitHub Actions secret for release builds.
# The placeholder below is a validly formatted but not-secret example key: it
# only satisfies ESPHome's format check for placeholder (PR/CI) builds.
api_encryption_key: "f0aQMe3RzMHKjV0COPgwXknBICzGef6+ejORSu9VVpM="
